{
  "version": 4,
  "name": "Senior Design - Cluster Layer",
  "description": "ESP32-WROOM 30-pin DevKit prototype; SX1278 connected through a labeled 8-pin harness (receiver / cluster).",
  "notes": "ASSEMBLY: Top/component-side view. Horizontal copper strips on underside; implement every shown cut. U1 assumes the built-in ESP32 DevKit V1 30-pin pinout: confirm your board labels and header spacing before soldering. Power U1 through USB with a stable 5 V supply; use its regulated 3V3 and common GND for the peripherals. Do not feed 5 V to SX1278 or the sensor AO. Verify the DevKit regulator can supply ESP32 plus LoRa peak current. J1 is a deliberately ordered 2.54 mm signal harness, NOT the physical SX1278 module footprint; connect each labeled signal to the corresponding label on your module. Keep SX1278 off-board at the J1 edge with a short harness, and place C1 (100 nF ceramic) and C2 (100 uF electrolytic, >=6.3 V) at the radio VCC/GND terminals; if the harness is longer, fit the capacitors directly at the module too. C2 positive to 3V3, negative to GND. Attach the correct antenna directly to the SX1278 RF/ANT connector before transmitting; no RF trace on this stripboard. DIO1-DIO5 unused. Check continuity and absence of 3V3-to-GND shorts before power-up.",
